  "Specification": "This module models a small instance of the Yo-Yo distributed algorithm (without pruning) on a fixed graph of five nodes and a specific set of edges. The state is described by four variables: phase, incoming, outgoing, and mailbox, which together capture the local state and message buffers of each node. The module includes a temporal property AllPermanentlyDown, which asserts that eventually, all nodes will remain in the 'down' phase forever. The PostCondition operator encodes a counterexample trace as a sequence of states and actions, likely for model checking or debugging purposes. The module instantiates the YoYoNoPruning module, and the comments suggest that larger graphs can be used by uncommenting and modifying the Nodes and Edges definitions.",
